  "query_preview": "..\nTonight to Friday: Mild, dry weather dominates. A ridge builds \nin this weekend; a system tracks into B.C. Monday to dampen it, \nbefore rebuilding into Thursday. Expect variable mid to high \nclouds. Some models track a wave and shower threat by the Blues \nto Camas Prairie Monday; consensus has PoPs less than 10%, but \nwe will monitor it. Southwest winds increase over the basin \nMonday PM, gusting 15-20 mph with RHs in the lower 20s; the HDWI\npeaks above the 95th percentile, so there's slightly elevated \nfire wx concerns then. A system approaches Friday, with Cascade\nand eastern WA/ID shower threat and breezy winds in the afternoon.\nYet PoPs are only around 20%. Lows are mostly in the 40s, some \n50s near Wenatchee, deep basin and L-C Valley and upper 30s \nmountain valleys. Highs in the 70s to mid-80s through Thursday, \nwith Monday warmest; Friday upper 60s and 70s. /Solveig",
